Hello,

You're receiving this email because you subscribed to Chicago street sweeping alerts through <%= ENV["SITE_NAME"] %> (<%= ENV["SITE_URL"] %>) for <%= @street_address.presence || @area.name %>.

The City has extended street sweeping through Dec. 17—about a month past its usual Thanksgiving cutoff—to catch lingering leaves (Sun-Times, Nov. 19: https://chicago.suntimes.com/news/2026/11/19/chicago-extends-street-sweeping-to-week-before-christmas-as-leaves-linger-on-city-trees). Extra sweeps will be scheduled ad hoc based on weather and crew capacity.

When we reached out to the City's Open Data team, they informed us that the Department of Streets and Sanitation will NOT be updating the 2026 schedule dataset (https://data.cityofchicago.org/Sanitation/Street-Sweeping-Schedule-2026/u5ai-3efk/about_data) that powers <%= ENV["SITE_NAME"] %>. Unfortunately, this means that schedules and email alerts here will miss those extra sweeps.

Through Dec. 17, please watch for temporary orange signs on your block.
<% if @ward_office %>

Have feedback about late-season sweeping and the lack of a reliable schedule? Consider letting your alderperson know:

Ward <%= @ward_office[:ward] %> — Alderperson <%= @ward_office[:alderperson] %>
<% if @ward_office[:phone] %>Phone: <%= @ward_office[:phone] %><% end %>
<% if @ward_office[:email] %>Email: <%= @ward_office[:email] %><% end %>
<% if @ward_office[:website] %>Website: <%= @ward_office[:website] %><% end %>
<% else %>

Have feedback about late-season sweeping and the lack of a reliable schedule? Consider contacting your alderperson (https://www.chicago.gov/city/en/about/wards.html) and asking for a permanently extended schedule.
<% end %>
<%= render "shared/email_footer",
      disclaimer: true,
      manage_url: @manage_url,
      unsubscribe_url: @unsubscribe_url %>
